{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104055","id":2389305358,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6OaegO","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104055/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104055/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/1b1ab76a14d4521583825df059f88eaaaa5c573c","number":104055,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Core: Add `FixedVector` template - a collection that can be used completely on the stack.","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is a high performance `Vector`-like object. In practice, we can use it to reduce the number of per-frame allocations throughout Godot.\r\n\r\nIn particular, `FixedVector` is useful if the maximum number of objects is small and known, and the objects are needed only temporarily. It could also be used to return a small, uncertain number of objects from a function in a performant fashion if the maximum is known.\r\n\r\nThe class can be expanded with more useful functions in the future as needed.\r\n\r\n## Comparisons\r\n`FixedVector` is designed to be as easily exchangeable for [`Vector`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/templates/vector.h) and [`LocalVector`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/templates/local_vector.h) as possible. This can be most easily achieved through [`Span`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/templates/span.h) interfaces.\r\n\r\n`FixedVector` is similar to 3.x' [`FixedArray`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/3.x/core/fixed_array.h), but some decisions about its design are different.\r\n`FixedVector` is similar to [`std::array`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array), but it supports adding and removing objects, and a number of other goodies (like conversion to `Span`).\r\n`FixedVector` is somewhat similar to [`StringBuffer`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/string/string_buffer.h), but focuses on being a general purpose collection and does not support arbitrary expansion into the heap.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{